      "id": "OQ-B3AEC-001",
      "q": "CHK-001 lists process-fact-registry/process-fact-levels as modify targets. Confirm those files are changed only for CHK-002 gate-consumed candidate artifact/mode semantics, while host availability, launcher readiness, startup timing, and execution diagnostics remain runtime facts and are not promoted into process-fact evidence.",
      "evidence": "AGENTS.md separates runtime/environment facts from the process registry; host readiness and executable behavior are runtime facts. CHK-001 and CHK-002 currently share the registry files in their modify lists.",
      "sourcePointers": [
        "docs/requirements/decisions/workflow-convergence-failure-remediation-execution-plan.md#7.2",
        "docs/requirements/decisions/workflow-convergence-failure-remediation-execution-plan.md#7.4",
        "CHK-001",
        "CHK-002"
      ],
      "resolution": "Per Workstream B sections 7.2 and 7.4, CHK-001 launcher readiness, first-output timing, total timeout, kill/reap, and capacity release remain runtime/execution facts and do not become new process gate evidence. CHK-002 may update process-fact registry and its verifier only when the signed candidate artifact or rollout-mode fields consumed by scope/review gates change.",
      "resolvedAt": "2026-07-17T08:58:30.428Z"
    }
  ]
